From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:33:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): view and edit session labels, and default labels
 per project

Sessions carry user labels (tags), but the web UI had no way to see or
change them, a label could not be deleted through the API, and projects
had no way to tag the sessions created in them.

Server:
- PATCH /v1/sessions/{id} deletes a label whose value is null. Reserved
  and cost_control.* keys are rejected for a delete exactly as for a set;
  the empty-string clear for omni_project and the pin key is unchanged.
- Session create in a project merges the project's config.labels under
  the request's labels (request wins). Internal, over-length and
  non-string entries are skipped, and the merged labels still pass the
  reserved-label checks. Imports into a project get them too. Labels apply
  only at creation, not when a session is moved into a project later.
- A create with apply_project_labels: false takes its labels as the
  final set, so a default removed for one session isn't added back.

Web:
- A Labels section in the session info popover lists user labels and,
  with edit access, adds, edits and removes them, with inline validation
  of the key (128) and value (256) column widths. Internal labels
  (omnigent.*, cost_control.*, omni_project) stay hidden.
- Project settings gain a "Default labels" editor using the same
  LabelEditor component, stored as config.labels. A label still typed in
  the add row is saved with the dialog, and an invalid one blocks Save
  with its inline message.
  "Add" there only edits the draft, so closing the dialog with unsaved
  label changes warns once before discarding them.
- The project settings dialog is capped to the viewport (85dvh): its
  fields scroll while the header and Save/Cancel stay visible, since the
  labels editor made it taller than short windows. Upstream PR #5194
  targets the same problem there.
- The new-session composer's "+" menu gains Labels, opening the same
  editor for the session about to be created, with or without a project.
  A project's defaults are filled in, marked "from project", and
  removable for that session only. The labels show as chips in the
  composer and go with the create request.
- The list-cache overlay is shared by title, archive and label updates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit f0c4dfa6e1d6acc3b386c7f3582fee2c233454ba)
